 "notes": [
  "Quantity: s_open = a_open - b_open at 15m bar open, converted to pips (EURUSD/GBPUSD pip=0.0001, USDJPY pip=0.01). No prices, returns, premiums or PnL computed anywhere in this census.",
  "Timestamps are UTC (parquet ts, tz=UTC); London hour is the bar-open instant converted to Europe/London via stdlib zoneinfo (BST/GMT handled by the tz database, correct across all DST transitions 2021-2026 in-corpus).",
  "Day-sets per pair per corpus: trading day = calendar day with ANY bar of that month; ME1 = last such day of month, ME2 = last two, MID = days 13-16 of each month (calendar, not re-based on bars).",
  "Percentile convention: linear interpolation on the sorted sample (numpy default 'linear'): h=(n-1)q; v = v[floor(h)] + (h-floor(h))*(v[floor(h)+1]-v[floor(h)]). Values reported in pips rounded to 4 decimals.",
  "n_nonpos = count of s_open <= 0 in the bucket (non-positive spread).",
  "rollover_21_22UTC = bars opening 21:00-21:59 UTC, all days (reference bucket per plan section 6).",
  "fixcert composite per pair: entry_F-1h = bars opening London 14:00-15:59 on ME1|ME2 days; exit_fix = bars opening 16:00 London on ME1|ME2 days. Cost law: spread per DISTRIBUTION OF FILL x k in {1.0,1.5,2.0}; commission/slippage remain DECLARED_UNMEASURED.",
  "Verdict-law note (plan section 6): this census measures the fix-window/month-end cost bucket that FIXCERT was killed against via session-bucket proxies; it sharpens the owner packet and does NOT rescue mechanism A (kill is ancestry/class + frontier, not cost-only).",
  "Sources are Dukascopy M1 bid/ask derived 15m bars (single-source panel, paper tier): EURUSD from FX-RANGEFADE-2M-SHADOW-V1 shadow worktree, GBPUSD/USDJPY from FX-MAJORS-SEARCH-V1 worktree (read-only public data). Fill quality on M1 bid/ask is unmeasurable: no volume/depth/tape."
 ]
